 ## Independent asks and review handoffs (deadlock.5)
 
-The board records every `REQUEST:` in a Dev/Browser PM/PO post as its own ask, including each numbered item in a multi-ask post, and shows them under OPEN ASKS on every turn. A newer event does not close or replace an older ask. Close an ask only with a typed `ask_dispositions` entry: `pin` (full 40-hex candidate in evidence), `hold` (exact reason, dependency and owner), `po_decision`, `completed` or `superseded` (each with a link, comment id or SHA). A generic reply, an unrelated action, or the fact that your reply was published does not close an ask. An overdue ask gets one recovery wake; if it is still open after that, it becomes a board blocker and you receive no further wakes for it. An unrelated PR HOLD does not block an independent ask.
+The board records every `REQUEST:` in a Dev/Browser PM/PO post as its own ask, including each numbered item in a multi-ask post, and shows them under OPEN ASKS on every turn. A newer event does not close or replace an older ask. Close an ask only with a typed `ask_dispositions` entry: `pin` (full 40-hex candidate in evidence), `hold` (exact reason, dependency and owner), `po_decision`, `completed` or `superseded` (each with a link, comment id or SHA). A held ask stays open until its exact named release event is evidenced; then use `reopen` with that exact `release_event` and a source link/comment ID/SHA so it returns to pending for fresh disposition. A generic reply, an unrelated action, or the fact that your reply was published does not close or release an ask. An overdue ask gets one recovery wake; if it is still open after that, it becomes a board blocker and you receive no further wakes for it. An unrelated PR HOLD does not block an independent ask.
 
 To answer an ask by handing work to a Dev, return the handoff in `review_handoffs` and an `ask_dispositions` entry with `disposition=dispatched` and `review_handoff_index` pointing at it. The ask stays open (dispatched) until the owner's receipt arrives; a handoff without a receipt gets one recovery wake, then becomes a board blocker.
 
